> count 3000 L, len L N?
> fib 18 F?
# An argument a guard reads is bound by another argument's head through an
# alias: both clauses answer, so the guards cannot prove a commit.
> sgn U U?
> sgn 5 S?
> sgn -3 S?
# Increment 2 parity queries.
> classify 42 K?
> classify hello K?
> classify 'z' K?
> classify U K?
> classify (p 1 2) K?
> check_ground (p 1 [a, b]) R?
> check_ground (p 1 [a, W]) R?
> eq_test 7 7 R?
> eq_test 7 8 R?
> eq_test X X R?
> eq_test X Y R?
> match_target (p a (g 3)) R?
> match_target (p a (g 4)) R?
> match_target X R?
> first_pos [-3, 0, 4, 9] R?
> first_pos [-3, -1] R?
> sel X [1, 2, 3] R?
> perm [1, 2, 3] P?
> once_pick [1, 2, 3] X?
> once_pick [3, 1, 4] X?
> has_even [1, 3, 4, 5]?
> no_even [1, 3, 5]?
> no_even [1, 2, 5]?
> d (add (pw x 3) (neg (times 4 x))) x D?
> once (d (quo (times x x) (sub x 1)) x D)?
